wmenu
=====

WARNING: AI-GENERATED CODEBASE
------------------------------
This AI-generated version needs human review, testing, and maintenance.
It is stable enough for everyday use, but not independently audited.

A small Win32 picker for newline-separated input. Inspired by LinArcX's
original wmenu: https://github.com/LinArcX/wmenu

Build
-----
Use a Visual Studio Developer Command Prompt and run make.

Credits
-------
Original wmenu by LinArcX; thanks for the inspiration.

How it works
------------
wmenu is a GUI filter: newline-separated stdin goes in, the selected line is printed to stdout.

Examples:

```
dir /b | .\wmenu.exe
where.exe *.exe | .\wmenu.exe -p run:
dir /b | .\wmenu.exe -c -w 800 -l 12
```

Useful flags:

```
-p text             prompt text
-e utf8|ansi|oem    stdin/stdout/prompt encoding; default utf8
-x px -y px -w px   position and width
-c                  center window
-l lines            visible list lines; -l-1 fills the screen (default 5)
-m                  select multiple entries; Ctrl+Enter adds one, Enter finishes
-i                  ignore ASCII case while matching
-V                  enable vi support; Ctrl+Alt+V toggles vi mode
-d                  use normal Windows edit shortcuts instead of emacs-ish keys
-b                  exit when focus leaves the window
-fn name -fs pt -fw weight
                    font face, size, and weight
-v                  print version
-h                  print usage
```

Clearing the search returns to the first row. Ctrl+O/I revisits previous
searches and selected lines; typing/refining one search is treated as one
location. History keeps the latest 128 positions.

Default keys:

```
Enter       print selection and exit
Esc         exit (vi insert mode: return to normal mode)
Up/Down     move list selection
Ctrl+N/P    next/previous item
Ctrl+D/U    page down/up
Ctrl+O/I    back/forward through visited searches and rows
Ctrl+A      move to start; press again at start to select all
Ctrl+E      move to end
Ctrl+K      delete to end
Ctrl+W      cut selection
Ctrl+Backspace delete previous word
Ctrl+Alt+V  toggle vi mode
```

See HACKING for code layout and release notes.

